# ONE LINE ENDING, AND IT IS LF.
#
# This repo was nine files of CRLF, sixteen of LF and a .gitignore that was
# both. That is not cosmetic here: patches are applied to these files by exact
# string match, and a script that assumed the wrong one computed its offsets
# against the wrong line length and cut 33KB out of the Caddyfile.
#
# text=auto eol=lf normalises on commit and checks out LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe is the one interpreter with real superstitions about this.
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never touched.
*.webm binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png  binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.mp3  binary
*.m4a  binary
